+# Accordion Tools v0.20.0 — Rhythm Trainer and shared notation
+
+Release date: November 9, 2026
+
+## What's new
+
+### Bass–Treble Rhythm Trainer
+
+- A dedicated two-hand coordination tool with independently selectable Stradella accompaniments and treble rhythmic templates in 2/4, 3/4, 4/4, and 6/8.
+- Treble playback follows the root of each chord in the shared harmonic-progression catalog; exercises can span longer progressions.
+- A synchronized two-lane timeline highlights attacks as they sound, displaying four bars per row on desktop. The compact Stradella and treble diagrams highlight their active buttons together.
+- Optional music notation is available through the top toolbar and right-side notation panel.
+- Includes a Cueca reference rhythm derived from the ABC Player's two-hand examples, plus 2/4 and 4/4 marches and 3–2 / 2–3 Son and Rumba clave exercises.
+
+### Consistent Stradella notation
+
+- A common notation mapper is shared by the Rhythm Trainer, Bass Pattern Player, recorded sequences, and applicable Progression Assistant displays.
+- Written bass and preset-chord note positions no longer change with the instrument's configured audio register.
+- Standard symbolic Stradella notation, repeated chord-quality labels, and optional counterbass markings are controlled through common settings.
+- The Progression Assistant can switch between standard button notation and an expanded sounding-pitch view.
+- Ordinary, imported ABC scores retain their written notation.
+
+### Bass Pattern Player rhythm review
+
+- Audited the full built-in 29-pattern catalog for metrical validity and multi-bar timing.
+- Corrected the compressed 12/8 Shuffle, the incomplete two-bar Bo Diddley figure, and the meter/timeline of the standard African bell pattern.
+- Normalized five-stroke Son and Rumba clave patterns to their two-bar 3–2 / 2–3 structures.
+- Documented stylistic arrangements that may have multiple accepted realizations in [the rhythm audit](docs/internal/bass-pattern-rhythm-audit.md).
+
+### Interface and documentation
+
+- Rhythm Trainer appears immediately above ABC Player in the tool list; notation visibility is controlled from the top toolbar.
+- Updated six-language interface labels and the application's user/developer documentation.
+
+## What remains planned
+
+- Guided tapping with per-hand accuracy feedback, and treble arpeggio exercises, are not yet part of this release.
+
+## Release verification
+
+Before tagging and publishing, run `npm run verify:release`, `npm run test:e2e`, and a manual browser playback/notation check on Windows. GitHub Pages builds the site from the `main` branch after a push.
